Aim
To simulate an airline passenger processing system using GPSS.

Theory
An Airline Passenger Processing System is used to model passenger movement through airport activities such as check-in, security checking, and boarding.
Passengers arrive at the airport and first enter the check-in queue. After check-in, they move to the security checking area and finally proceed towards the boarding gate.
The GENERATE block creates passengers. The QUEUE block manages passenger waiting lines. The SEIZE block allocates resources such as check-in counters and security counters.
The ADVANCE block represents processing time at each stage. The RELEASE block frees the resources after service completion.

This simulation helps in analyzing:

Passenger waiting time
Check-in counter utilization
Security system performance
Airport operational efficiency

Applications:

Airport management systems
Passenger flow analysis
Transportation systems
Security management systems

Conclusion

Thus, the simulation of an airline passenger processing system was successfully implemented using GPSS. 
The experiment helped in understanding passenger movement through different stages of airport processing and analyzing resource utilization.
